module String exposing (String)

{-| The opaque scalar type for text.

The full `String` module — `isEmpty`, `append`, `split`, `toUpper` and the rest of Elm's
functions over it — is not ported yet; `String.ignored` beside this file is the port's
reference. Nothing in the language writes a `String` literal yet either (see
`docs/spec/lexical-structure.md`'s *Strings* section), so today a `String` reaches a program
only as a value a JavaScript facade wrapper hands back, the way `Failure`'s two constructors
will each carry one (`docs/spec/evaluation-semantics.md`).

# Strings
@docs String
-}

type String = String -- NOTE: The compiler provides the real implementation.
